},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"MEDIUM","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"medium"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-04-08T13:55:00.729Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-04-08t13:55:00.729z"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-24T06:08:14.136Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-24t06:08:14.136z"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"description","object":"A container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain Ansible Automation Platform images. This issue arises from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during the build process. In certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. This vulnerability allows an attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary UID, including UID 0, gaining full root privileges within the container.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain ansible automation platform images. this issue arises from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during the build process. in certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. this vulnerability allows an attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary uid, including uid 0, gaining full root privileges within the container."},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.16","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.16"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-57847","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansib